From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:24:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: aop_audio: Offer only the float format the AOP
 delivers

aop_pcm_open() describes the microphone PCM as FLOAT_LE only, then
passes it through snd_dmaengine_pcm_refine_runtime_hwparams(), which
adds every format whose physical width the DMA channel can move. The
PCM therefore advertised S8 to DSD, and a capture opened as S16 or S32
got the AOP's float samples reinterpreted as integers: a stuck constant
on the M1 Pro and garbage on the J616s.

Keep only FLOAT_LE after the refinement, as t8140_aop_audio.rs already
does. Applications that want an integer format get it converted by
alsa-lib's plug layer or PipeWire.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 580a7c820b4ad16cd51ade1b97cf4c6417997b70)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs b/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
index f1eb26f460..28de9cabc4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
@@ -839,6 +839,13 @@ unsafe extern "C" fn aop_pcm_open(substream: *mut bindings::snd_pcm_substream) -
         dev_err!(data.dev, "Unable to refine hwparams");
         return ret;
     }
+    // The refinement adds every format whose sample width the DMA channel can move, but the
+    // AOP always delivers 32-bit floats: keep only those.
+    hwparams.formats &= bindings::BINDINGS_SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_FLOAT_LE;
+    if hwparams.formats == 0 {
+        dev_err!(data.dev, "The DMA channel cannot carry 32-bit samples");
+        return EINVAL.to_errno();
+    }
     unsafe { (*(*substream).runtime).hw = hwparams };
     let ret = unsafe { bindings::snd_dmaengine_pcm_open(substream, dma_chan) };
     if ret < 0 {
